{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of upward momentum: When sentiment history shows a cluster of positive values (1.00) following a price dip, the model's linear extrapolation fails to capture the subsequent spike; apply a +10% to +15% upward adjustment to the first 5-7 days of the forecast.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion after peaks: The model consistently fails to anticipate the sharp reversal from highs (e.g., ~80 EUR) to lows (e.g., ~63 EUR); reduce forecast values by 15-20% starting 10 days after a local maximum, regardless of sentiment.",
    "Ignore sentiment lag in volatility regimes: Positive sentiment scores often precede price drops in this dataset (e.g., Dec 2023); do not rely on recent positive sentiment to sustain upward forecasts if the price trend has already peaked.",
    "Adjust for flat-line bias: The model predicts near-constant growth or stagnation; replace the flat tail of the forecast with a decaying curve that aligns with the historical volatility range (approx. 63-76 EUR) rather than the model's projected 70-77 EUR ceiling.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: For the 30-day horizon, the model's error grows linearly; apply a non-linear decay factor to the forecast slope, reducing the projected daily increase by 50% to account for the observed rapid mean reversion."
  ]
}
